The three JSON files in this directory are vendored verbatim from the bambuddy
server's frontend, which generates them from OrcaSlicer's own PrintConfig.cpp
and Tab.cpp via scripts/generate-slicer-schema.mjs.

    source:  https://github.com/maziggy/bambuddy
             frontend/src/data/slicer/
    commit:  7c117dc6bc5ffef66aa81b8ea23619a386e22285
    date:    2026-08-10
    version: APP_VERSION = 1.2.6b1

They are a copy of a copy: when OrcaSlicer changes an option, the server
re-vendors and this directory has to follow, or the process-settings screen
writes values the slicer no longer honours.

To re-vendor (the maintainer's server clone lives at reference/bambuddy):

    cp reference/bambuddy/frontend/src/data/slicer/process-schema.json \
       reference/bambuddy/frontend/src/data/slicer/process-ui-tree.json \
       reference/bambuddy/frontend/src/data/slicer/process-toggle-rules.json \
       assets/slicer/

then update the commit/date/version above and run `flutter test
test/core/slicer/`. Those tests assert the invariants the screen depends on —
schema/tree key parity in both directions and no option type the codec cannot
serialise — so a re-vendor that adds an option the app cannot render fails there
rather than in front of a user.

See docs/plans/16-slicer-process-overrides.md §4.
